# Bigint power without overflow limit

Raises 2 to the 130th power to verify exponentiation produces a 40-digit
result far beyond 128 bits. The exponent is bigint as well: the type has
no mixed-type operations.

>>> source
base: bigint = 2
exponent: bigint = 130

power: bigint = base ** exponent
print(power)

<<< stdout
1361129467683753853853498429727072845824

<<< stderr
